IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa4-appointment.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 10, Chapter 1: Appointment (continued):
-- ss 157 to 161 (minimum age; disqualified persons; appointment of directors of a public company voted on
-- individually; validity of acts of directors), lines 2090-2154 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- ss 161A to 167F (lines 2155-2181) are shown repealed or blank in the text: coverage rows only, no code.
--
-- SOURCE and HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa4-requirements.l4 (a converter's plain-text rendering, not the
-- official text; JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered"; a caller must never
-- turn NOTHING into FALSE). Every branch carries its FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment.
-- Naming: every top-level name begins with the label of the provision it implements.

-- ---- s 157: minimum age for appointment as director ----------------------------------------------------------

-- "attained the age of 16 years": on the sixteenth anniversary of the date of birth (the text does not say how
-- a 29 February birthday is counted: fork F11). The day tested is the day the appointment takes effect (s 157(2)).
-- src:2090 | 157 Minimum age for appointment as director
-- src:2091 | (1) A person may not be appointed a director of a company unless he has attained the age of 16 years.
-- src:2099 | (6) This section has effect subject to section 158 (power to provide for exceptions from minimum age requirement).
@ref s 157(1), (6) Minimum age for appointment as director (src:2090-2091 and src:2099)
GIVEN person IS A Individual
      `the day the appointment takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the case is one in which regulations under section 158 allow a person who has not attained the age of 16 years to be appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157(1) section 157(1) bars the appointment of the person as a director` MEANS
    IF `the day the appointment takes effect` AT LEAST (`add years` (person's `date of birth`) 16)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person may not be appointed a director of a company unless he has attained the age of 16 years."
    ELSE IF `the case is one in which regulations under section 158 allow a person who has not attained the age of 16 years to be appointed`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "This section has effect subject to section 158"; the regulations are not among the sources
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2): an appointment made before the person is 16 but not to take effect until the person is 16 is not affected.
-- src:2092 | (2) This does not affect the validity of an appointment that is not to take effect until the person appointed attains that age.
@ref s 157(2) An appointment that does not take effect until the person attains that age (src:2092)
GIVEN person IS A Individual
      `the day the appointment is made` IS A DATE
      `the day the appointment takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157(2) section 157 does not affect the validity of the appointment made before the person attains the age of 16 years` MEANS
    IF       `the day the appointment is made` LESS THAN (`add years` (person's `date of birth`) 16)
         AND `the day the appointment takes effect` AT LEAST (`add years` (person's `date of birth`) 16)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This does not affect the validity of an appointment that is not to take effect until the person appointed attains that age"

-- (3): the bar is "not effective ... until he attains the age of 16 years": the function says whether the appointment
-- to the other office CANNOT YET make the person a director (the ruling of 2026-11-05 on "until" bars).
-- src:2093 | (3) Where the office of director of a company is held by a corporation sole, or otherwise by virtue of another office, the appointment to that other office of a person who has not attained the age of 16 years is not effective also to make him a director of the company until he attains the age of 16 years.
@ref s 157(3) Office of director held by virtue of another office (src:2093)
GIVEN `the office of director of the company is held by a corporation sole, or otherwise by virtue of another office` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Individual
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157(3) the appointment to the other office cannot yet make the person a director of the company` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the office of director of the company is held by a corporation sole, or otherwise by virtue of another office`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the office of director of a company is held by a corporation sole, or otherwise by virtue of another office"
    ELSE IF `the day in question` LESS THAN (`add years` (person's `date of birth`) 16)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not effective also to make him a director of the company until he attains the age of 16 years"

-- src:2094 | (4) An appointment made in contravention of this section is void.
@ref s 157(4) An appointment in contravention is void (src:2094)
GIVEN `the answer under section 157(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157(4) the appointment made is void` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 157(1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appointment made in contravention of this section is void"; the section's bar does not apply, so it says nothing of the appointment
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the appointment contravenes the section turns on regulations under section 158

-- src:2095 | (5) Nothing in this section affects any liability of a person under any provision of the Companies Acts if he—
-- src:2096 | (a) purports to act as director, or
-- src:2097 | (b) acts as a shadow director,
-- src:2098 | although he could not, by virtue of this section, be validly appointed as a director.
@ref s 157(5) Liability of a person who purports to act as director or acts as a shadow director (src:2095-2098)
GIVEN `the person purports to act as director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as a shadow director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person could not, by virtue of section 157, be validly appointed as a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157(5) section 157 leaves the person's liability unaffected` MEANS
    IF (`the person purports to act as director` OR `the person acts as a shadow director`) AND `the person could not, by virtue of section 157, be validly appointed as a director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if he— (a) purports to act as director, or (b) acts as a shadow director, although he could not, by virtue of this section, be validly appointed as a director"

-- ---- s 158: power to provide for exceptions from minimum age requirement ---------------------------------------
-- Subsections (1), (2), (4) and (5) are the regulation-making power: machinery (no function). (3) says what happens to
-- a person appointed by virtue of the regulations when the specified circumstances or conditions fail.

-- src:2103 | (3) If the specified circumstances cease to obtain, or any specified conditions cease to be met, a person who was appointed by virtue of the regulations and who has not since attained the age of 16 years ceases to hold office by virtue of that appointment.
@ref s 158(3) The person ceases to hold office when the circumstances or conditions cease (src:2103)
GIVEN `the person was appointed by virtue of regulations under section 158` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the specified circumstances have ceased to obtain, or a specified condition has ceased to be met` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Individual
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 158(3) the person has ceased to hold office by virtue of that appointment` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person was appointed by virtue of regulations under section 158` AND `the specified circumstances have ceased to obtain, or a specified condition has ceased to be met`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the specified circumstances cease to obtain, or any specified conditions cease to be met, a person who was appointed by virtue of the regulations"
    ELSE IF `the day in question` LESS THAN (`add years` (person's `date of birth`) 16)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who has not since attained the age of 16 years"

-- src:2104 | (3A) Nothing in subsection (3) affects any liability of a person under any provision of the Companies Acts or any other enactment, if, having ceased to hold office by virtue of that subsection, the person—
-- src:2105 | (a) purports to act as director, or
-- src:2106 | (b) acts as shadow director.
@ref s 158(3A) Liability of a person who has ceased to hold office (src:2104-2106)
GIVEN `the person has ceased to hold office by virtue of subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person purports to act as director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as shadow director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 158(3A) section 158(3) leaves the person's liability unaffected` MEANS
    IF `the person has ceased to hold office by virtue of subsection (3)` AND (`the person purports to act as director` OR `the person acts as shadow director`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if, having ceased to hold office by virtue of that subsection, the person— (a) purports to act as director, or (b) acts as shadow director"

-- ---- s 159 (existing under-age directors) is shown repealed or blank in the text: no code. ----------------------

-- ---- s 159A: disqualified person not to be appointed as director ------------------------------------------

-- The table in subsection (2) is data: twelve rows (six per Part), each a circumstance in column 1 and, in column 2,
-- the provision by virtue of which a permission, a licence or an exception can apply. The next declarations are
-- generated from the text lines (work/build.py).
-- src:2121 | For those purposes a person (P) is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation if: | Except in the application of the provision in relation to P acting in a capacity, or doing anything, for which P has the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or in respect of which an exception applies, by virtue of:
-- src:2122 | Part 1: England and Wales and Scotland
-- src:2123 | P is subject to a disqualification order or undertaking under the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986. | Section 1(1), 1A(1) or 9B(4) of the 1986 Act.
-- src:2124 | Any of the circumstances mentioned in section 11 of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 (bankruptcy etc) apply to P. | Section 11 of the 1986 Act.
-- src:2125 | P is subject to director disqualification sanctions within the meaning of section 11A of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986. | Section 15(3A) of the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018 (exceptions and licences).
-- src:2126 | Section 12 of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 (disabilities on revocation of administration order against an individual) applies to P. | Section 12 of the 1986 Act.
-- src:2127 | P is subject to a disqualification order or undertaking mentioned in section 12A or 12B of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 (recognition of Northern Ireland disqualification orders and undertakings). | Section 12A or 12B of the 1986 Act.
-- src:2128 | P is disqualified as mentioned in section 1184(2)(a) or (b) or is subject to a disqualification undertaking under section 1184(3). | Section 1184(5).
-- src:2129 | Part 2: Northern Ireland
-- src:2130 | P is subject to a disqualification order or undertaking under the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (S.I.2002/3150 (N.I. 4)). | Article 3(1), 4(1) or 13B(4) of the 2002 Order.
-- src:2131 | Any of the circumstances mentioned in Article 15 of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (bankruptcy etc) apply to P. | Article 15 of the 2002 Order.
-- src:2132 | P is subject to director disqualification sanctions within the meaning of Article 15A of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002. | Section 15(3A) of the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018 (exceptions and licences).
-- src:2133 | Article 16 of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (disabilities on revocation of administration order against an individual) applies to P. | Article 16 of the 2002 Order.
-- src:2134 | P is subject to a disqualification order or undertaking mentioned in Article 17 of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (recognition of GB disqualification orders and undertakings). | Article 17 of the 2002 Order.
-- src:2135 | P is disqualified as mentioned in section 1184(2)(a) or (b) or is subject to a disqualification undertaking under section 1184(3). | Section 1184(5).
@ref s 159A(2) The table of the directors disqualification legislation (src:2121-2135)
DECLARE `s 159A(2) Part of the table` IS ONE OF
    `s 159A(2) Part 1`
    `s 159A(2) Part 2`

-- One constructor per row of the table: six in Part 1 (England and Wales and Scotland), six in Part 2 (Northern Ireland).
@ref s 159A(2) The table (src:2121-2135)
DECLARE `s 159A(2) row of the table` IS ONE OF
    `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 1: a disqualification order or undertaking under the 1986 Act`
    `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 2: the circumstances in section 11 of the 1986 Act (bankruptcy etc)`
    `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 3: director disqualification sanctions (section 11A of the 1986 Act)`
    `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 4: section 12 of the 1986 Act (revocation of administration order against an individual)`
    `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 5: an order or undertaking mentioned in section 12A or 12B of the 1986 Act`
    `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 6: disqualified as mentioned in section 1184`
    `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 1: a disqualification order or undertaking under the 2002 Order`
    `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 2: the circumstances in Article 15 of the 2002 Order (bankruptcy etc)`
    `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 3: director disqualification sanctions (Article 15A of the 2002 Order)`
    `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 4: Article 16 of the 2002 Order (revocation of administration order against an individual)`
    `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 5: an order or undertaking mentioned in Article 17 of the 2002 Order`
    `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 6: disqualified as mentioned in section 1184`

@ref s 159A(2) The table (src:2121-2135)
GIVEN row IS A `s 159A(2) row of the table`
GIVETH A `s 159A(2) Part of the table`
`s 159A(2) the Part of the table in which the row appears` MEANS
    CONSIDER row
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 1: a disqualification order or undertaking under the 1986 Act` THEN `s 159A(2) Part 1`
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 2: the circumstances in section 11 of the 1986 Act (bankruptcy etc)` THEN `s 159A(2) Part 1`
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 3: director disqualification sanctions (section 11A of the 1986 Act)` THEN `s 159A(2) Part 1`
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 4: section 12 of the 1986 Act (revocation of administration order against an individual)` THEN `s 159A(2) Part 1`
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 5: an order or undertaking mentioned in section 12A or 12B of the 1986 Act` THEN `s 159A(2) Part 1`
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 6: disqualified as mentioned in section 1184` THEN `s 159A(2) Part 1`
    OTHERWISE `s 159A(2) Part 2`

-- Column 1 of each row, copied from the text by work/build.py (lines 2123-2128 and 2130-2135).
@ref s 159A(2) The table (src:2121-2135)
GIVEN row IS A `s 159A(2) row of the table`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 159A(2) the circumstance in column 1 of the row` MEANS
    CONSIDER row
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 1: a disqualification order or undertaking under the 1986 Act` THEN "P is subject to a disqualification order or undertaking under the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 2: the circumstances in section 11 of the 1986 Act (bankruptcy etc)` THEN "Any of the circumstances mentioned in section 11 of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 (bankruptcy etc) apply to P."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 3: director disqualification sanctions (section 11A of the 1986 Act)` THEN "P is subject to director disqualification sanctions within the meaning of section 11A of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 4: section 12 of the 1986 Act (revocation of administration order against an individual)` THEN "Section 12 of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 (disabilities on revocation of administration order against an individual) applies to P."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 5: an order or undertaking mentioned in section 12A or 12B of the 1986 Act` THEN "P is subject to a disqualification order or undertaking mentioned in section 12A or 12B of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 (recognition of Northern Ireland disqualification orders and undertakings)."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 6: disqualified as mentioned in section 1184` THEN "P is disqualified as mentioned in section 1184(2)(a) or (b) or is subject to a disqualification undertaking under section 1184(3)."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 1: a disqualification order or undertaking under the 2002 Order` THEN "P is subject to a disqualification order or undertaking under the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (S.I.2002/3150 (N.I. 4))."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 2: the circumstances in Article 15 of the 2002 Order (bankruptcy etc)` THEN "Any of the circumstances mentioned in Article 15 of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (bankruptcy etc) apply to P."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 3: director disqualification sanctions (Article 15A of the 2002 Order)` THEN "P is subject to director disqualification sanctions within the meaning of Article 15A of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 4: Article 16 of the 2002 Order (revocation of administration order against an individual)` THEN "Article 16 of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (disabilities on revocation of administration order against an individual) applies to P."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 5: an order or undertaking mentioned in Article 17 of the 2002 Order` THEN "P is subject to a disqualification order or undertaking mentioned in Article 17 of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (recognition of GB disqualification orders and undertakings)."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 6: disqualified as mentioned in section 1184` THEN "P is disqualified as mentioned in section 1184(2)(a) or (b) or is subject to a disqualification undertaking under section 1184(3)."
    OTHERWISE ""

-- Column 2 of each row: the provision by virtue of which a permission, licence or exception can apply.
@ref s 159A(2) The table (src:2121-2135)
GIVEN row IS A `s 159A(2) row of the table`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 159A(2) the provision in column 2 of the row` MEANS
    CONSIDER row
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 1: a disqualification order or undertaking under the 1986 Act` THEN "Section 1(1), 1A(1) or 9B(4) of the 1986 Act."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 2: the circumstances in section 11 of the 1986 Act (bankruptcy etc)` THEN "Section 11 of the 1986 Act."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 3: director disqualification sanctions (section 11A of the 1986 Act)` THEN "Section 15(3A) of the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018 (exceptions and licences)."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 4: section 12 of the 1986 Act (revocation of administration order against an individual)` THEN "Section 12 of the 1986 Act."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 5: an order or undertaking mentioned in section 12A or 12B of the 1986 Act` THEN "Section 12A or 12B of the 1986 Act."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 1 row 6: disqualified as mentioned in section 1184` THEN "Section 1184(5)."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 1: a disqualification order or undertaking under the 2002 Order` THEN "Article 3(1), 4(1) or 13B(4) of the 2002 Order."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 2: the circumstances in Article 15 of the 2002 Order (bankruptcy etc)` THEN "Article 15 of the 2002 Order."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 3: director disqualification sanctions (Article 15A of the 2002 Order)` THEN "Section 15(3A) of the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018 (exceptions and licences)."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 4: Article 16 of the 2002 Order (revocation of administration order against an individual)` THEN "Article 16 of the 2002 Order."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 5: an order or undertaking mentioned in Article 17 of the 2002 Order` THEN "Article 17 of the 2002 Order."
    WHEN `s 159A(2) Part 2 row 6: disqualified as mentioned in section 1184` THEN "Section 1184(5)."
    OTHERWISE ""

-- A fact about one row: whether P is in the circumstance of column 1, and whether, for the capacity P acts in or the
-- thing P does, P has the permission of a court or the authority of a licence or an exception applies by virtue of
-- column 2 ("Except in the application of the provision in relation to P acting in a capacity, or doing anything, ...").
@ref s 159A(2) The table (src:2121-2135)
DECLARE `s 159A(2) fact about a row` HAS
    row IS A `s 159A(2) row of the table`
    `P is in the circumstance in column 1` IS A BOOLEAN
    `P has the permission or authority, or an exception applies, by virtue of the provision in column 2` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Part 1 is for a company registered in England and Wales or Scotland, or for delivery of a document to the registrar
-- for England and Wales or Scotland; Part 2 is for Northern Ireland: the place of registration selects the Part.
-- src:2114 | (2) In the table—
-- src:2115 | (a) Part 1 defines “disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation” for the purposes of provisions of this Act so far as relating to—
-- src:2116 | (i) a company registered in England and Wales or Scotland, or
-- src:2117 | (ii) the delivery of a document to the registrar of companies for England and Wales or Scotland or a statement contained in such a document;
-- src:2118 | (b) Part 2 defines “disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation” for the purposes of provisions of this Act so far as relating to—
-- src:2119 | (i) a company registered in Northern Ireland, or
-- src:2120 | (ii) the delivery of a document to the registrar of companies for Northern Ireland or a statement contained in such a document.
-- src:2121 | For those purposes a person (P) is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation if: | Except in the application of the provision in relation to P acting in a capacity, or doing anything, for which P has the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or in respect of which an exception applies, by virtue of:
@ref s 159A(2) The directors disqualification legislation (src:2114-2121)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A `s 159A(2) Part of the table`
`s 159A(2) the Part of the table that applies for the place` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN `s 159A(2) Part 2`
    OTHERWISE `s 159A(2) Part 1`

-- src:2112 | 159A Disqualified person not to be appointed as director
-- src:2113 | (1) A person may not be appointed a director of a company if the person is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation (see subsection (2)).
-- src:2114 | (2) In the table—
-- src:2115 | (a) Part 1 defines “disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation” for the purposes of provisions of this Act so far as relating to—
-- src:2116 | (i) a company registered in England and Wales or Scotland, or
-- src:2117 | (ii) the delivery of a document to the registrar of companies for England and Wales or Scotland or a statement contained in such a document;
-- src:2118 | (b) Part 2 defines “disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation” for the purposes of provisions of this Act so far as relating to—
-- src:2119 | (i) a company registered in Northern Ireland, or
-- src:2120 | (ii) the delivery of a document to the registrar of companies for Northern Ireland or a statement contained in such a document.
-- src:2121 | For those purposes a person (P) is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation if: | Except in the application of the provision in relation to P acting in a capacity, or doing anything, for which P has the permission of a court or the authority of a licence, or in respect of which an exception applies, by virtue of:
-- src:2122 | Part 1: England and Wales and Scotland
-- src:2123 | P is subject to a disqualification order or undertaking under the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986. | Section 1(1), 1A(1) or 9B(4) of the 1986 Act.
-- src:2124 | Any of the circumstances mentioned in section 11 of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 (bankruptcy etc) apply to P. | Section 11 of the 1986 Act.
-- src:2125 | P is subject to director disqualification sanctions within the meaning of section 11A of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986. | Section 15(3A) of the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018 (exceptions and licences).
-- src:2126 | Section 12 of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 (disabilities on revocation of administration order against an individual) applies to P. | Section 12 of the 1986 Act.
-- src:2127 | P is subject to a disqualification order or undertaking mentioned in section 12A or 12B of the Company Directors Disqualification Act 1986 (recognition of Northern Ireland disqualification orders and undertakings). | Section 12A or 12B of the 1986 Act.
-- src:2128 | P is disqualified as mentioned in section 1184(2)(a) or (b) or is subject to a disqualification undertaking under section 1184(3). | Section 1184(5).
-- src:2129 | Part 2: Northern Ireland
-- src:2130 | P is subject to a disqualification order or undertaking under the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (S.I.2002/3150 (N.I. 4)). | Article 3(1), 4(1) or 13B(4) of the 2002 Order.
-- src:2131 | Any of the circumstances mentioned in Article 15 of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (bankruptcy etc) apply to P. | Article 15 of the 2002 Order.
-- src:2132 | P is subject to director disqualification sanctions within the meaning of Article 15A of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002. | Section 15(3A) of the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018 (exceptions and licences).
-- src:2133 | Article 16 of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (disabilities on revocation of administration order against an individual) applies to P. | Article 16 of the 2002 Order.
-- src:2134 | P is subject to a disqualification order or undertaking mentioned in Article 17 of the Company Directors Disqualification (Northern Ireland) Order 2002 (recognition of GB disqualification orders and undertakings). | Article 17 of the 2002 Order.
-- src:2135 | P is disqualified as mentioned in section 1184(2)(a) or (b) or is subject to a disqualification undertaking under section 1184(3). | Section 1184(5).
@ref s 159A(2) The directors disqualification legislation (src:2112-2135)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      facts IS A LIST OF `s 159A(2) fact about a row`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 159A(2) the person is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN f YIELD
                    `s 159A(2) the Part of the table in which the row appears` (f's row) EQUALS `s 159A(2) the Part of the table that applies for the place` place
                AND f's `P is in the circumstance in column 1`
                AND NOT (f's `P has the permission or authority, or an exception applies, by virtue of the provision in column 2`)) facts
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For those purposes a person (P) is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation if:"

-- (1): "may not be appointed ... if the person is disqualified": the bar. JUST TRUE = barred.
-- src:2112 | 159A Disqualified person not to be appointed as director
-- src:2113 | (1) A person may not be appointed a director of a company if the person is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation (see subsection (2)).
@ref s 159A(1) Disqualified person not to be appointed as director (src:2112-2113)
GIVEN `s 159A(2) the person is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 159A(1) section 159A(1) bars the appointment of the person as a director` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 159A(2) the person is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person may not be appointed a director of a company if the person is disqualified under the directors disqualification legislation"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is disqualified is a borrowed answer the caller has not given

-- src:2136 | (3) An appointment made in contravention of this section is void.
@ref s 159A(3) An appointment in contravention is void (src:2136)
GIVEN `the answer under section 159A(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 159A(3) the appointment made is void` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 159A(1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appointment made in contravention of this section is void"; the section's bar does not apply, so it says nothing of the appointment
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the appointment contravenes the section is not known

-- src:2137 | (4) Nothing in this section affects any liability of a person under any provision of the Companies Acts or any other enactment if the person—
-- src:2138 | (a) purports to act as director, or
-- src:2139 | (b) acts as shadow director,
-- src:2140 | although the person could not, by virtue of this section, be validly appointed as a director.
@ref s 159A(4) Liability of a person who purports to act as director or acts as shadow director (src:2137-2140)
GIVEN `the person purports to act as director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as shadow director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person could not, by virtue of section 159A, be validly appointed as a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 159A(4) section 159A leaves the person's liability unaffected` MEANS
    IF (`the person purports to act as director` OR `the person acts as shadow director`) AND `the person could not, by virtue of section 159A, be validly appointed as a director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the person— (a) purports to act as director, or (b) acts as shadow director, although the person could not, by virtue of this section, be validly appointed as a director"

-- ---- s 160: appointment of directors of public company to be voted on individually --------------------------

-- (3): a motion approving a person's appointment, or nominating a person for appointment, is treated as a motion for
-- his appointment.
-- src:2145 | (3) For the purposes of this section a motion for approving a person's appointment, or for nominating a person for appointment, is treated as a motion for his appointment.
@ref s 160(3) A motion for approving or nominating is treated as a motion for appointment (src:2145)
GIVEN `the motion is for approving a person's appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the motion is for nominating a person for appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(3) the motion is treated as a motion for the person's appointment` MEANS
    IF `the motion is for approving a person's appointment` OR `the motion is for nominating a person for appointment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "For the purposes of this section a motion for approving a person's appointment, or for nominating a person for appointment, is treated as a motion for his appointment"; any other motion is not addressed

-- (1), with (4): "must not be made unless a resolution that it should be so made has first been agreed to by the meeting
-- without any vote being given against it". JUST TRUE = the motion is barred.
-- src:2141 | 160 Appointment of directors of public company to be voted on individually
-- src:2142 | (1) At a general meeting of a public company a motion for the appointment of two or more persons as directors of the company by a single resolution must not be made unless a resolution that it should be so made has first been agreed to by the meeting without any vote being given against it.
-- src:2146 | (4) Nothing in this section applies to a resolution amending the company's articles.
@ref s 160(1), (4) Appointment of directors of public company to be voted on individually (src:2141-2142 and src:2146)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the motion is for the appointment of two or more persons as directors of the company by a single resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is one amending the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a resolution that the motion should be so made has first been agreed to by the meeting without any vote being given against it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(1) section 160(1) bars the motion being made` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is one amending the company's articles`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section applies to a resolution amending the company's articles."
    ELSE IF NOT (`s 4(2) the company is a public company` AND `the motion is for the appointment of two or more persons as directors of the company by a single resolution`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At a general meeting of a public company a motion for the appointment of two or more persons as directors of the company by a single resolution"
         ELSE IF `a resolution that the motion should be so made has first been agreed to by the meeting without any vote being given against it`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be made unless a resolution that it should be so made has first been agreed to by the meeting without any vote being given against it"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2), first sentence: a resolution moved in contravention is void, objected to or not.
-- src:2143 | (2) A resolution moved in contravention of this section is void, whether or not its being so moved was objected to at the time.
@ref s 160(2) A resolution moved in contravention is void (src:2143)
GIVEN `the answer under section 160(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(2) the resolution moved is void` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 160(1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution moved in contravention of this section is void"; the motion was not in contravention
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the motion contravened the section is not known

-- (2), second sentence: where such a resolution is passed, no provision for automatic reappointment applies.
-- src:2144 | But where a resolution so moved is passed, no provision for the automatic reappointment of retiring directors in default of another appointment applies.
@ref s 160(2) No automatic reappointment where a resolution so moved is passed (src:2144)
GIVEN `the resolution was moved in contravention of section 160 and was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(2) a provision for the automatic reappointment of retiring directors in default of another appointment applies` MEANS
    IF `the resolution was moved in contravention of section 160 and was passed`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no provision for the automatic reappointment of retiring directors in default of another appointment applies"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "But where a resolution so moved is passed"

-- ---- s 161: validity of acts of directors -----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The defects the section lists: "(a) that there was a defect in his appointment; (b) that he was disqualified from holding
-- office; (c) that he had ceased to hold office; (d) that he was not entitled to vote on the matter in question", and, by
-- subsection (2), that the resolution for his appointment is void under section 160.
DECLARE `s 161(1) defect discovered afterwards` IS ONE OF
    `s 161(1)(a) a defect in the person's appointment`
    `s 161(1)(b) the person was disqualified from holding office`
    `s 161(1)(c) the person had ceased to hold office`
    `s 161(1)(d) the person was not entitled to vote on the matter in question`
    `s 161(2) the resolution for the person's appointment is void under section 160`
    `s 161(1) another defect`

-- src:2147 | 161 Validity of acts of directors
-- src:2148 | (1) The acts of a person acting as a director are valid notwithstanding that it is afterwards discovered—
-- src:2149 | (a) that there was a defect in his appointment;
-- src:2150 | (b) that he was disqualified from holding office;
-- src:2151 | (c) that he had ceased to hold office;
-- src:2152 | (d) that he was not entitled to vote on the matter in question.
-- src:2153 | (2) This applies even if the resolution for his appointment is void under section 160 (appointment of directors of public company to be voted on individually).
@ref s 161(1) and (2) Validity of acts of directors (src:2147-2153)
GIVEN `the person was acting as a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      defect IS A `s 161(1) defect discovered afterwards`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 161(1) the acts of the person acting as a director are valid` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person was acting as a director`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The acts of a person acting as a director are valid"
    ELSE CONSIDER defect
         WHEN `s 161(1) another defect` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text lists four defects and the void resolution of section 160, and does not say "only"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

